From 366f6e2b9ee9275f9ffe7369be95af4ec7b03945 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 357/488] soh: name the 20 address-named symbols defined in
 z_player_lib.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 20 are defined in soh/src/code/z_player_lib.c; updating their references touches 6 files in total.

  * func_8008EC70 -> Player_ApplyHeldItemAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies heldItemAction into itemAction and
    switches the model group to match

  * func_8008EF30 -> Player_IsOnHorse
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns stateFlags1 & PLAYER_STATE1_ON_HORSE

  * func_8008EF44 -> Player_SetShootingGalleryAmmo
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stores ammo + 1 into
    play->shootingGalleryStatus

  * func_8008F128 -> Player_HoldsUnattachedHookshot
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when the hookshot is held and heldActor
    is NULL, i.e. the hook is not out

  * func_8008F2BC -> Player_ActionToSword
    deduced, confidence HIGH: maps an itemAction to a 0-2 sword index
    (PLAYER_IA_SWORD_CS is 0) or -1, in the style of
    Player_ActionToModelGroup

  * func_8008F87C -> Player_AdjustLegToFloor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: two-bone IK: raycasts the floor under the foot
    and bends the thigh, shin and foot joints onto it, spawning
    EffectSsGFire on hot floor types

  * func_800906D4 -> Player_UpdateMeleeWeaponQuads
    deduced, confidence HIGH: pairs the three tip positions with
    sMeleeWeaponBasePositions to update meleeWeaponInfo and the sword trail
    and quads

  * func_80091738 -> Player_LoadPauseModel
    deduced, confidence HIGH: DMAs gameplay_keep and the age-appropriate
    link object into a caller-supplied segment and inits the skeleton --
    called only by kaleido with pauseCtx->playerSegment

  * D_80126038 -> sLegIkThighOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-age Vec3f translation applied before the
    shin joint's rotation; x is the thigh length in model units (1304 adult,
    695 child)

  * D_80126050 -> sLegIkShinLengths
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-age translation from the shin joint out to
    the foot (1265 adult, 826 child)

  * D_80126058 -> sLegIkThighLengthSq
    deduced, confidence HIGH: SQ(13.04) and SQ(6.95) -- the thigh length in
    world units, squared, for the IK law of cosines

  * D_80126060 -> sLegIkLimbLengthSqDiff
    deduced, confidence HIGH: thigh squared minus shin squared per age
    (13.04^2 - 12.65^2 = 10.019, 6.95^2 - 8.26^2 = -19.925), the constant
    term of the same law of cosines

  * D_80126068 -> sLegIkFootHeightOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-age height added to the raycast floor Y
    before the leg is bent onto it

  * D_80126070 -> sFootprintOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: {0, -300, 0} in foot space, the point raycast
    down to place the footprint effect

  * D_80126080 -> sMeleeWeaponBladeTip
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tip of the blade line in hand space; its x is
    overwritten each frame with the held weapon's length

  * D_8012608C -> sMeleeWeaponQuad0Tip
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tip of the first sweep quad; its x tracks the
    blade length plus 1200 and the spin-attack stretch

  * D_80126098 -> sMeleeWeaponQuad1Tip
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tip of the second sweep quad, sharing
    sMeleeWeaponQuad0Tip's x

  * D_801260A4 -> sMeleeWeaponBasePositions
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the three base points paired with the tips
    above by Player_UpdateMeleeWeaponQuads

  * D_80126184 -> sHookshotAimOffset
    deduced, confidence GUESS: hand-space point transformed into
    Player.unk_3C8 while the hookshot or longshot is drawn; the field's
    meaning is not established, so the aim reading is inferred from the
    reticle branch it sits in

  * D_80126190 -> sHookshotHeadOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: hand-space point the held hookshot head actor
    is placed at while aiming

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
